      "message": "These comments can be wrong or stale. We probably want to use a macro which takes a temperature and returns temp_ratio:\n\n    #define TEMP_FAN_MAX 55\n    #define TEMP_FAN_OFF 30\n    #define TEMP_TO_RATIO(c) \\\n            ((c - TEMP_FAN_OFF) * 100 / (TEMP_FAN_MAX - TEMP_FAN_OFF))\n\nThen, we\u0027ll use:\n\n    .decreasing_temp_ratio_threshold \u003d TEMP_TO_RATIO(30),\n    .increasing_temp_ratio_threshold \u003d TEMP_TO_RATIO(37),\n\nA drawback is a bad value is not as obvious. For example, TEMP_TO_RATIO(60) is invalid since it exceeds 100%. I can\u0027t think of a smart way to catch it at compile time.\n\nWDYT?",
